  "title": "nvshmem triton kernels IMA silently",
  "issue_id": "163915",
  "bug_description": "### 🐛 Describe the bug\n\n### Repro\n```\nimport torch.symm_mem._nvshmem_triton as nvshmem\n\n@triton.jit\ndef foo(...):\n    nvshmem.get(...)\n\ndef run():\n    nvshmem.enable_triton()\n    foo[(1, )]()\n```\n\n### Cause\nThe previous `enable_triton` UI requires the user-defined Triton kernel have a \"nvshmem\" in its name. But this requirement is in the doc and sometimes the user does not notice it.\nIf users did not do so, the kernel would miss the NVSHMEM init, and silently hit CUDA IMA.\n\n### Versions\n\nmain\n\ncc @H-Huang @awgu @wanchaol @fegin @fduwjj @wz337 @wconstab @d4l3k @pragupta @ezyang @msaroufim @dcci",
